            "### 🔍 Detailed Radiological Findings & Observations\n"
            "- **Lungs & Airway**: Trachea is midline. Normal bronchovascular markings bilaterally without focal consolidation, pleural effusion, or pneumothorax.\n"
            "- **Cardiothoracic Ratio**: Heart size is within normal physiological limits (CTR < 0.50). Mediastinal and hilar contours are unremarkable.\n"
            "- **Costophrenic Angles**: Sharp and clear bilaterally without blunting.\n"
            "- **Osseous Structures**: Visualized thoracic cage, clavicles, and ribs are intact without focal lytic or blastic lesions.\n\n"
            "### 🩺 Primary Clinical Impression & Differential Diagnoses\n"
            "- **Impression**: No acute cardiopulmonary disease or active infiltrates identified.\n"
            "- **Differential Considerations**: Clinically clear chest radiograph. Low probability for acute bacterial pneumonia or congestive heart failure.\n\n"
            "### ⚠️ Severity Assessment & Urgency Stratification\n"
            "- **Risk Tier**: 🟢 Normal / Low Clinical Urgency\n\n"
            "### 📋 Recommended Diagnostic Next Steps & Follow-Up\n"
            "- Correlate with clinical presentation (auscultation, O2 saturation, fever profile).\n"
